hw/sh4: ze0 IPL patch file: join ROM image A to the kernel (TODO M8.C1d).

On the card the kernel (image B, file 0x3e00200) and the applications
(image A, file 0x200200: Navi.exe, AuiApp.exe, the *CC.dll screens, no
nk.exe) are separate Windows CE images.  The built-in loader puts both in
RAM, but nk.exe's OEMInit prints "Rom chain NOT found": its XIP-chain
pointer (a .data fixup, 0xffffffff on the card) is left for the IPL to
fill, and the IPL is not on the card.  Every application CreateProcessW
then fails with LastError 2.

New machine option ipl-patch=FILE: lines "PHYS HEXBYTES" ('#' comments)
that the IPL would leave in RAM.  A line inside a loaded image is written
into that image before it becomes a ROM blob; any other line becomes its
own ROM blob.  tools/ze0_ipl.py writes the file (XIPCHAIN block, chain
pointer in the kernel's .data template, ROMHDR ulRAMEnd below image A,
image A's DLL data reservation off, both TOCs compacted).  Nothing on the
-kernel file changes.


